    // ---- named from the engine's own weapon field table ----
    // acts.exe wfd reads the table the engine itself uses to resolve weapon.<field>: a name hash,
    // a type, an offset, a size and which struct it belongs to. That table is the complete list
    // of what the engine exposes - 407 fields here - so none of these is inferred from another
    // title or matched by value. The engine states the offset.
    //
    // Only the ones it gives a plain offset for are here. 132 of the 407 are computed by a getter
    // and have no offset at all; those still need matching against a dump. The one pair sharing an
    // offset is left out, being two tests of one value rather than two fields.
    //
    // The flags are a byte each and packed, so their offsets are not four-aligned. They read with
    // "form": "byte" - reading one as an int would take three neighbours with it.

    {"offset": "0x390", "name": "gadgetreadysound", "source": "engine", "kind": "hash", "form": "hash", "observed": 0, "examples": []},
